        "created_at": "2015-03-09T18:05:40.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Does anyone want to help me playtest it? Send me a PM. It's a game about building a machine for the 1900's World Fair. It's slightly silly, and I've only actually /played/ it out a few times so I'm sure it has lots and lots of bad interactions and problems to find out. It's also a lot of printing/cutting, with about 35 pages worth of cards to print/cut.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>It is for 2-6 players, and you'll need some kind of tokens to use that can be easily seen whose is whose (i use colored buttons - but i have a ton of those lying around for other reasons) - It should take probably about 15-30 minutes to play... i think. heh.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>either PM me your email or email me at lynkfox@gmail.com I can email the files to you (PDF) or i can link your gmail to them in my gdrive. If you aren't interested, no hard feelings :)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>(edit: added information)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Oh, and I'd hope you'd give me feedback ;) No hard feelings if you think its stupid either, or if you find major game breaking problems. I'm not married to any of this thing (and its already gone through a few different design iterations) just hope for some constructive feedback!</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:44:11.374Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
