        "raw": "<p>Does anyone want to help me playtest it? Send me a PM. It&#39;s a game about building a machine for the 1900&#39;s World Fair. It&#39;s slightly silly, and I&#39;ve only actually /played/ it out a few times so I&#39;m sure it has lots and lots of bad interactions and problems to find out. It&#39;s also a lot of printing/cutting, with about 35 pages worth of cards to print/cut.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>It is for 2-6 players, and you&#39;ll need some kind of tokens to use that can be easily seen whose is whose (i use colored buttons - but i have a ton of those lying around for other reasons) - It should take probably about 15-30 minutes to play... i think. heh.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>either PM me your email or email me at lynkfox@gmail.com I can email the files to you (PDF) or i can link your gmail to them in my gdrive. If you aren&#39;t interested, no hard feelings :)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>(edit: added information)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Oh, and I&#39;d hope you&#39;d give me feedback ;) No hard feelings if you think its stupid either, or if you find major game breaking problems. I&#39;m not married to any of this thing (and its already gone through a few different design iterations) just hope for some constructive feedback!</p>",
