        "id": 136947,
        "name": "lynkfox",
        "username": "lynkfox",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lynkfox/{size}/1997_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-03-09T18:48:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>its 2-6 players, competitive, but with centralized decks. &nbsp;Not a deck builder, but it borrows from some concepts that deckbuilders use (central row, resource management)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Players have pick resources off Location cards (in a center row), which are used to play Operations cards from their hands (Drawn from a single community deck) - these cards either are events or parts, and the goal is to get the most points out of your parts by the time someone completes a Machine. Machines are completed by having 1 of each of the 5 needed parts in play.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>and Donner, this is in such very early phases of testing, that it's gonna be going on for a long while. You can always bug me at a later date when you have the resources to print it out :)</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:13:13.893Z",
